  "notes": "Strip is mostly estates, cemetery ground, Mill Creek, the B&O railroad and the old canal bed: only three crossings. Knowlton Street meets Crawford Avenue from the west; the plate is cut just east of Crawford so whether it continues is not shown. Crawford Avenue ends at Spring Grove Avenue (north side; a streetcar wye sits in the mouth). Lafayette Avenue merges into McAlpin Avenue at a very acute angle at the bottom-left plate corner; the pick is where the centrelines converge, right at the plate edge, uncertain by 30 px or more along McAlpin. Lafayette's west side between about y 4650 and y 6900 is the plate cut itself, so its bends are read from the cut and the inner line."
